# Stop the docked S Pen from waking the tablet a second after it suspends.
#
# The pen is a power_supply, and power_supply_register() marks every supply as a
# system wakeup source.  While the pen sits in its silo charging, the driver
# reports charge changes, and each power_supply_changed() counts as a wakeup
# event: measured on hardware, one every ~20 s with the tablet idle and nothing
# else firing.  Suspend therefore ended almost as soon as it began -- entry and
# exit one second apart -- and pressing the power key again just repeated it.
#
# The pen's own dock GPIO is not the culprit and is left alone: across a
# suspend cycle its interrupt count did not move while the power_supply wakeup
# counter did.
#
# A charging accessory has no business waking the tablet, so the supply keeps
# reporting its state -- the battery indicator still works -- but stops being a
# reason to come out of suspend.  The proper fix is no_wakeup_source in the
# driver's power_supply_desc, which needs a kernel; this needs a reboot at most.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="power_supply", KERNEL=="gts9u-spen", ATTR{power/wakeup}="disabled"
